    "content": "Rain is liquid water that condenses from atmospheric vapor and falls to Earth when droplets become too heavy, occurring when temperatures are above freezing. It is a vital component of the water cycle, providing essential moisture for ecosystems and agriculture. Rain forms at weather fronts, along mountains, or through convection. This video explains the three types of rainfall:43sMr CognitoYouTube • Jan 30, 2019 43s Key information about rain: Measurement: Light rain is <0.10is less than 0.10<0.10 inches per hour, moderate is 0.100.100.10 to 0.300.300.30 inches, and heavy is >0.30is greater than 0.30>0.30 inches per hour. Formation: Water vapor condenses around particles like dust or pollen in clouds before falling, according to the National Environmental Satellite, Data, and Information Service (.gov). Types: Major types include convective (from rising hot air), orographic (over mountains), and frontal (at weather fronts). Regional Forecast: A clipper system is expected to bring a mix of rain and snow to the Northeast US this weekend, according to The Weather Channel. Other meanings for \"Rain\" include: Rain (entertainer): A South Korean singer and actor, according to Wikipedia. Rain (app): A financial platform for earned wage access, says www.rain.app.com. RAIN (mindfulness): An acronym for a meditation practice (Recognize, Allow, Investigate, Nurture), notes Tara Brach. Rain (wildfire): An autonomous wildfire management technology, according to www.rain.aero.",
